{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773441663,"nonce":"hbMCvaDtJ3M92/JAITmLBN7yh3c=","title":"Chat follow-ups: transcript rehydration, terminal fallback, Gemini, model picker","message":"## Problem\nThe first chat-first pass fixed rich Claude chat and cross-linking to History, but several UX and state-management gaps remain.\n\nCurrent regressions or missing pieces:\n- Live chat tabs do not rehydrate prior transcript history, so reopening or revisiting an existing session can still show 'No events' even when History has the full conversation.\n- The debug terminal view duplicates or drifts when toggled repeatedly, and it does not provide a reliably aligned alternative view of the same active chat.\n- Gemini is missing from the New Agent Chat backend choices.\n- The chat view does not expose model selection as a first-class UI control.\n- History transcript rows are too tall because selection affordances consume a separate visual line.\n\n## Context\nThe intended product direction is still chat-first, with terminal as optional fallback/debug rather than a coequal transport. If the terminal cannot remain meaningfully aligned with live chat state, it should degrade gracefully instead of implying stronger synchronization than it actually offers.\n\n## Scope\n- Rehydrate rich-chat transcript state from stored conversation history when resuming/opening sessions\n- Resolve or disable the misleading debug terminal affordance\n- Add Gemini to backend selection if the existing integration path supports it cleanly\n- Add a first-class model-selection UI in the chat header/status area\n- Tighten History transcript layout so selection controls do not double row height\n- Validate the resulting UX in Playwright\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}